                <pb facs="0519" n="511" xml:id="pg511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/11558: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-01">June 1, 1941</date>.<lb/>[Received June 2—3:15
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. Abdul Illah returned Baghdad today and resumed regency. Senior Iraq military
                    and civil officials and notables and British Ambassador and myself met him
                    several miles outside Baghdad and drove with him to his palace where he received
                    other members Diplomatic Corps and other welcoming personages. Regent expressed
                    sincere appreciation to me personally. New government will be formed
                    tonight.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
